# Multiple bundles

OKMate can keep several knowledge trees configured. It does not merge them
into one catalog. `check`, `inspect`, `search`, and `build` stay single-root.

## List, then inspect one path

```sh
okmate roots --format paths
```

```sh
okmate roots --format paths | while IFS= read -r root; do
  okmate inspect --profile strict catalog "$root"
done
```

If the config is missing or `roots` is empty, `./knowledge` is printed when
that directory exists.

## Sync git roots

```sh
okmate roots --format json --no-sync
okmate sync
```

`--sync` (the default for some listings) fetches configured git roots first.
`--no-sync` prints what is already resolved.

## What this is not

There is no merged cross-root search, no hosted query API, and no MCP server
in the shipped binary. Those appear in landscape notes as boundaries, not
features.
